SUMMARY:[現場] The Poetic and the Photographic: A Conversation between Ja
 son Francisco and Alexander Nemerov
LOCATION:McMurtry Building\, Oshman Hall
URL:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-poetic-and-the-photographic-a-con
 versation-between-jason-francisco-and-alexander-nemerov
DESCRIPTION:https://events.stanford.edu/event/the-poetic-and-the-photograph
 ic-a-conversation-between-jason-francisco-and-alexander-nemerov\n\nJoin ph
 otographer Jason Francisco and art historian Alexander Nemerov as they dis
 cuss their new publication\, Autobiography of an Unknown American\, a book
  of Francisco’s photographs\, made and found at various sites across the
  contemporary United States\, accompanied by Nemerov’s poems.\n\nThe boo
 k is a field guide to the lost corners of America\, a book of lamentation 
 and praise\, a sustained encounter with the sorrow that American civilizat
 ion shelters within itself—a dialogue of aftermaths and reckonings.  \n\
 nJason Francisco is an artist and essayist who joins documentary and conce
 ptual art\, focusing on questions of historical memory and witness. Franci
 sco’s large-scale projects include the book Alive and Destroyed: A Medit
 ation on the Holocaust in Time. He is a professor at Emory University.\n\n
 Alexander Nemerov is the author of many books on American art and culture\
 , including Fierce Poise: Helen Frankenthaler and 1950s America and The Fo
 rest: A Fable of America in the 1830s. He is the Carl and Marilynn Thoma P
 rovostial Professor in the Arts and Humanities at Stanford University.\n\n
 Photo credit: Alex Ramos\n\nVISITOR INFORMATION\nOshman Hall is located in
  the McMurtry Building on Stanford campus at 355 Roth Way. Visitor parking
  is free after 4pm on weekdays\, except by the Oval. Alternatively\, take 
 the Caltrain to Palo Alto Transit Center and ride the free Stanford Margue
 rite Shuttle. If you need a disability-related accommodation or wheelchair
  access information\, please contact Julian
